			)
		)
		(uuid "34cee62b-140b-4964-b94a-72ca0c3e7a2e")
	)
	(text "R1/R2/R3 = 47R limit LED peak current next to strong readers (0R gave 60-110 mA\npeaks in simulation); they cost ~5 mV at the lighting threshold.\nC3/C6 are DNP trim positions. Tune with a NanoVNA + sniffer loop, or by\nswapping C2/C5 until the LED lights at maximum distance."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 187.96 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "4aed41f8-1a52-4517-927b-365a17933417")
	)
	(text "UHF 860-960 MHz channel - lights D4 (red)\nMeander dipole -> C7 -> 1SS351 Greinacher voltage doubler -> C8 -> R3 + D4.\nUHF_GND is just the dipole's left arm; the card has no global ground.\nThe dipole is deliberately long: the diode pair is capacitive (~1.7 pF), so the\ndetector peaks above the dipole's own resonance (see scripts/uhf_match.py)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 137.16 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "6220f360-3365-4848-a0b0-aa05dae0e88e")
	)
	(text "125 kHz (LF) channel - lights D1 (amber)\nL1 || C1 + C2 (+C3 trim) resonate at 125 kHz. The LED rectifies the tank\nvoltage itself. Simulated LED reverse voltage reaches 3.6-5 V in very strong\nfields (LED rating is typically 5 V): rev B should add an antiparallel diode."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 35.56 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "af153a45-9582-4f15-a00d-940636a93701")
	)
	(text "13.56 MHz (HF/NFC) channel - lights D2 (green)\nL2 || C4 + C5 (+C6 trim) resonate at 13.56 MHz incl. ~25 pF LED/stray C."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 86.36 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ee800d29-41ce-400a-9cdc-e531e8cdde9f")
	)
